# DISABLED 2026-09-02 — both rules are commented out on purpose. Do not re-enable them here.
#
# This file was written when the app was hosted on Cloudflare PAGES, where a _redirects file is how
# you get a single-page-app fallback. The app is no longer a Pages site: wrangler.jsonc deploys a
# WORKER that serves ./dist itself, and the Worker-assets platform validates this file and REFUSES
# THE WHOLE DEPLOY if it disagrees with it. Both rules below are rejected:
#
#   `/api/*  /api/:splat  404`   -> 404 is not a valid status for a rule (200/301/302/303/307/308)
#   `/*      /index.html  200`   -> read as an infinite loop, because the rule would re-trigger
#
# Neither is needed. wrangler.jsonc already does both jobs, and does them properly:
#
#   "not_found_handling": "single-page-application"   -> unknown paths serve index.html (incl. /try)
#   "run_worker_first": ["/api/*"]                    -> /api/* reaches the Worker, not the assets
#
# Kept as a file rather than deleted so the next person who wonders where the SPA fallback lives
# finds this note instead of writing the same broken rules again.
#
# The original, for the record:
#   /api/*   /api/:splat   404
#   /*       /index.html   200
